WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.870
- House, I'm challenging you

00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:04.257
to not flinch during my reaction video.

00:00:04.257 --> 00:00:05.590
Pewoop!

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:06.870
- Still drawing those lines,

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:08.563
instead of looking at the cards.

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:11.448
(Adam moaning)

00:00:11.448 --> 00:00:12.740
(cup clanking)

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:13.573
- More juice?

00:00:14.777 --> 00:00:16.801
- If he wants more juice,
he has to ask for it.

00:00:16.801 --> 00:00:18.510
(Adam choking)

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:19.343
- He's choking.

00:00:19.343 --> 00:00:20.980
- Time to institute the Heimlich maneuver

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:23.090
and stop bullying your child.

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:23.973
- It's impossible, it's mac and cheese.

00:00:23.973 --> 00:00:26.020
- What do you mean it's impossible?

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.561
What, is mac and cheese unchokable?

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:31.170
(Adam screaming)

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:32.400
All right, the fact that he's yelling

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:33.850
though, makes it a little bit less likely

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:34.850
that he's actually choking.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:36.580
If you're yelling, that
means you're moving air.

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:39.980
- 10-year-old boy, screams
for his life for no reason.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:42.710
- He's autistic, severely autistic.

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:44.450
- Okay, so a child with autism,

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:47.760
what we have is an
Autism Spectrum Disorder.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:49.010
And, we don't know where

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:50.650
in that spectrum, this child lies.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.840
- [Foreman] Can't talk,
can't make eye contact.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:54.950
Screaming's probably his
way of communicating.

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.240
- Yeah, you know, some children

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.550
that have been diagnosed with
autism, one of the challenges

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:01.460
that they face is verbal and
non-verbal communication.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:04.440
But, some children don't have
good social cue identification

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.100
where they can't understand
someone's emotion

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.360
by reading their body language,

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:08.810
or they can't speak themselves

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:10.460
or they choose not to speak themselves.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:11.930
- His brain can't filter information.

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:13.590
It's a constant assault on his senses.

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:14.990
I'd, scream too.

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:17.410
- One of the main things
that go hand-in-hand

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.312
with ASD, hypersensitivity, sometimes

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.250
to light, touch, sound.

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:24.140
And remember, while we're
only naming the challenges,

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:26.220
there are some positives that can come

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:28.030
from a diagnosis of ASD.

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:31.010
Some children are super
smart, some have the ability

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:34.140
to memorize things way better
than the average child.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:35.910
So, it's not only about the challenges,

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:37.310
it's about the strengths too.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:39.620
- ER checked his throat,
no obstructions, nothing,

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:41.290
which means the only symptom was a scream,

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:42.790
which is diagnostic of nothing.

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:44.460
- I completely agree with Foreman.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:47.010
You have a child who is
diagnosed with autism,

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:48.170
who started screaming,

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:49.940
and the parents are very worried about it.

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:51.910
And now, they're doing this giant workup

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:53.040
with multiple specialists.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.240
I wouldn't even know what
the consultation would ask

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:56.140
of the specialist.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:58.700
- A stool sample to check
for parasites, blood culture

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:01.360
to rule out infection, and ANA for lupus.

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:02.460
- Because he screamed?

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:04.220
- I love investigating,

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:06.270
if there is an investigation warranted.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:09.070
You're checking for ova
and parasites and lupus?

00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:10.870
You can't order tests willy-nilly

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:13.140
because false positives
are really a thing.

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:16.020
- Dust, wheat, pollen,
a toxin, or something-

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:17.320
- It could literally be anything!

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:19.630
'Cause right now, your
one symptom is screaming.

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:21.490
- Run a lung ventilation scan.

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:22.810
Lungs are in the chest too, right?

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:24.340
- I had a date last night, she screamed.

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:26.780
Should we spend $100,000 testing her?

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:27.770
- Why did your date scream?

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:29.243
That was a weird revelation.

00:02:29.243 --> 00:02:32.360
- Of course not, this isn't
a veterinary hospital, zing!

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:34.130
- Actually, the veterinary
hospital thing is kind

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:37.100
of funny to me, because in
medicine we oftentimes say,

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:38.670
treating kids, working

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:41.020
in pediatrics, is a lot like being a vet.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:42.450
Because, sometimes the children,

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:44.550
if they're really young,
can't tell you what's wrong

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:47.300
with them, so it's almost
like treating a dog

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.880
who can't tell you what's
wrong with them either.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:49.713
- You know what it's gonna be like

00:02:49.713 --> 00:02:52.350
trying to put an autistic
kid into a nuclear scanner?

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:53.350
I don't envy you guys.

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:55.460
- In those cases, we do sedate.

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:57.920
We give medications like benzodiazepines

00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:59.195
for temporary sedation.

00:02:59.195 --> 00:03:00.470
(Adam screaming)

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:01.303
- [Mother] Can't you
sedate him or something?

00:03:01.303 --> 00:03:03.180
- I could if I don't want the test results

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:04.073
to mean anything.

00:03:04.073 --> 00:03:05.180
- Are they doing a CT?

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:07.630
If they're doing a CT, you
could sedate the child.

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:08.463
I don't know why you said

00:03:08.463 --> 00:03:10.643
that the test won't mean anything.

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:16.070
God, did they just break

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:18.200
into people's homes all the time?

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:23.120
- Big shocker, dad's depressed.

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:25.790
- And they're, getting
information on the parents!

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:27.463
This is so unethical.

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:35.630
This workup on a screaming
child is gonna cost $10 million.

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:38.850
They're gonna test his
sand out of his sandbox!

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:40.430
Who's paying for this?

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:41.620
I can't get insurers

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.550
to pay for an antibiotic if it comes

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:45.270
in an easy-to-swallow capsule,

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:46.530
and they're gonna get insurance

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:48.830
to pay for sand testing, shamone!

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:51.210
- Fecal matter, is there
a sample we can look at?

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:53.560
- Parents have the smear
kit, the kid is constipated.

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:55.810
- Go up his rear and get a smear.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:58.070
- Talk about creating
a traumatic situation

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:01.000
for a child for absolutely
zero reason at this time.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.800
But somehow, 'cause it's
a House M.D. episode,

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:04.140
he's gonna be right.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:05.830
I don't even know what they're
looking for in this sphere.

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:08.030
They already got an ova
and parasite sample.

00:04:09.253 --> 00:04:10.569
(Adam retching)

00:04:10.569 --> 00:04:11.474
- [Father] Adam?

00:04:11.474 --> 00:04:12.630
- Adam?

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:14.073
Adam?

00:04:14.073 --> 00:04:17.320
(Adam retching)

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:20.940
- So, what makes fluid fill
the lining of the kid's lungs?

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:23.000
- Infection, tumor (chuckles).

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.300
I feel like I'm one of his
students just yelling stuff out.

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:26.690
- If there's a pleural effusion, we have

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:27.760
to rule out heart failure.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:29.950
The pleura, by the way, is the lining

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:31.200
that covers the lungs.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:34.240
Organs are covered by pleural membranes,

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:36.470
which essentially prevents the organs

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:38.090
from rubbing all over each other.

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:40.430
So, there's a cardiac membrane,
there's a lung membrane.

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:41.994
- [House] Get the kid an echocardiogram.

00:04:41.994 --> 00:04:43.881
(Adam screaming)

00:04:43.881 --> 00:04:44.714
- Adam?

00:04:44.714 --> 00:04:47.060
- Very hard to perform an echo as is,

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:49.360
but to perform one on
a uncooperative patient

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:51.548
or a combative patient, even harder.

00:04:51.548 --> 00:04:54.215
(Adam grunting)

00:04:59.381 --> 00:05:00.670
- What?

00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:02.170
What is it, is his heart okay?

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:04.293
- No.

00:05:04.293 --> 00:05:07.890
Echo suggested a conduction
abnormality, EKG confirmed it.

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:09.680
- A conduction abnormality is basically

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:10.530
when there's a problem

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:12.590
with electrical conductivity of the heart.

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:15.290
So basically, in one part of
your heart you have a node

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:16.730
that starts your cardiac rhythm.

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:18.680
And then, it travels throughout
the rest of the heart.

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:19.827
The reason it has to travel

00:05:19.827 --> 00:05:21.820
throughout this conductive system, is

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:22.653
because you don't want

00:05:22.653 --> 00:05:24.900
the entire heart, beating simultaneously.

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:26.802
Otherwise, it's gonna have
all the blood just splat

00:05:26.802 --> 00:05:28.330
against each other.

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:30.470
But, if you have the top
of the heart beat first

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:32.420
and then the bottom of the heart beats,

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:35.500
then you can have a rhythmical
pulsation of the blood

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:36.333
throughout the heart.

00:05:36.333 --> 00:05:37.556
- Get a lung biopsy.

00:05:37.556 --> 00:05:38.620
- What, it took a half an hour

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:40.160
to get the mask on the
kid for the lung scan!

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:42.410
- Oh, I'm sorry, was there
somewhere you needed to be?

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:43.750
- What are they gonna do, a bronchoscopy?

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:45.540
I don't understand how they're
gonna do a lung biopsy,

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:47.370
like interventional radiology?

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:49.090
What part of the lung are they gonna test?

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:50.770
This makes no sense, this is brutal.

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:52.730
- We wanna do a lung biopsy.

00:05:52.730 --> 00:05:54.350
- Lung biopsies usually
come back negative.

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:56.307
So, biopsy a lymph node under the arm.

00:05:56.307 --> 00:05:59.057
(Adam screaming)

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:04.260
- Why are they against
sedating this poor child?

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:08.070
Sedate, please, it will not
change your biopsy results.

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:10.880
And, the child will not
be further traumatized

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:12.560
by this medical experience.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:15.210
- Hope is what's making it miserable.

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:17.460
What they should do, is
get a Cocker Spaniel.

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:21.130
Dog would look him in
the eye, wag his tail

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:21.963
when he's happy.

00:06:21.963 --> 00:06:23.610
- Animal therapy for children

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:25.630
with autism can actually
be quite beneficial.

00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:27.160
There's less judgment that comes

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:29.060
from animals, almost
no judgment, actually.

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:30.500
The interaction that you could have

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:32.410
with the animal is so much simpler.

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:35.810
That is an easier introduction
to human interaction,

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:37.180
which is much more complex.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:38.820
Horses, dogs, that kind of thing,

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:41.150
supportive animals really go a long way

00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:42.260
for children who have autism.

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:43.800
Not for all, but in some cases.

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:48.660
- No cancer, because
these aren't lymph cells.

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:49.493
- Then, what are they?

00:06:49.493 --> 00:06:51.300
- Okay, let me try and guess.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:54.330
These aren't lymph cells, so
what did he get a biopsy of?

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:57.860
A huge sweat gland, an
abscess, a dermatofibroma?

00:06:57.860 --> 00:06:59.160
Oh my God, what could have he gotten?

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:02.470
Oh, oh a teratoma, that has hair cells

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:03.870
in, ah, I can't, I have no idea.

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:04.990
- Liver cells?

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:07.060
- Does he have liver cancer
that has metastasized

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:07.893
to his armpit?

00:07:07.893 --> 00:07:09.320
- What's the difference
between cancer cells

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:10.460
and liver cells?

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:12.800
Why can one pass through
walls, but the other can't?

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:13.894
- Cancer cells are damaged, lets them grow

00:07:13.894 --> 00:07:15.607
into blood vessels, go wherever they want.

00:07:15.607 --> 00:07:17.440
- So, if the liver cells are damaged...

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:19.230
- Liver isn't damaged,
the tests were normal.

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:21.300
- Well, tests on a liver being normal,

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:23.170
doesn't necessarily mean
the liver is normal.

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:25.840
Because, the tests that we
use to check liver function

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:27.280
which we call liver function tests,

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:28.350
it's actually a misnomer.

00:07:28.350 --> 00:07:31.610
They're actually liver inflammation tests

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:33.550
that tell us if the liver is damaged,

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:35.770
thereby releasing liver enzymes.

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:37.230
And, if these liver enzymes are elevated

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:38.490
that we know there's a
problem with the liver.

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:41.150
However, if your liver is so diseased

00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:43.650
that it's in the
end-stage of liver cancer,

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:46.300
cirrhosis, those numbers can be normal

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:48.050
because your liver is almost fried

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:49.520
and there's no enzymes left to be had.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:51.963
- It's not his liver,
his heart or his lungs.

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:55.360
It's the calcium carbonating in his stool.

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:57.690
- Kid was constipated, parents
probably just overdid it.

00:07:57.690 --> 00:08:02.100
- Maybe, he ate a bunch of chalk, or Tums.

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:04.310
- Or they didn't do it at all.

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:06.410
Calcium carbonate's also what's in chalk.

00:08:06.410 --> 00:08:07.351
- Oh!

00:08:07.351 --> 00:08:08.704
- So, he ate some chalk, it isn't toxic.

00:08:08.704 --> 00:08:10.600
Sure it didn't cause a pleural effusion.

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:13.390
- Forget the chalk, this kid's got pica.

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:15.510
Take him into a buffet,
he's gonna eat the table.

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:18.980
- Pica, it's a condition
where, you start eating things

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:21.850
that are not edible, paint
off of the walls, mud.

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:24.033
- Show me what you ate.

00:08:30.076 --> 00:08:32.743
(Adam groaning)

00:08:36.618 --> 00:08:37.451
- Adam?

00:08:37.451 --> 00:08:38.385
- Honey?

00:08:38.385 --> 00:08:39.218
Adam?

00:08:39.218 --> 00:08:40.660
- I don't know what that
was, some kind of sand fly

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:43.680
or sand weasel inside of that sand.

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:46.110
- It's a micro tumor, started in his lung

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:47.500
which caused a pleural effusion.

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:48.910
Then it metastasized to his liver

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:50.030
which made it slough cells.

00:08:50.030 --> 00:08:52.340
- No, it has to be some
kind of worm traveling

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:53.892
throughout his body.

00:08:53.892 --> 00:08:57.475
(light instrumental music)

00:08:59.210 --> 00:09:00.360
- Hey, kill the lights.

00:09:03.746 --> 00:09:05.246
He's seeing them all the time.

00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:07.643
- What are you looking for?

00:09:07.643 --> 00:09:09.190
- He's telling us what he was seeing,

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:10.720
telling us exactly what was wrong

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:13.973
with him, drawing them for
us over and over again.

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:16.400
Hello my pretties.

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:17.240
- Nematodes!

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:20.330
- [House] It's not a
tumor Foreman, it's worms.

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:21.310
- Aha, we said worm!

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:22.530
We also said everything else.

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:24.190
So, I'm not gonna even take credit for it.

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:26.720
- Animal makes potty in the sandbox,

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:29.731
boy plays in the sandbox,
boy eats the sand,

00:09:29.731 --> 00:09:31.970
you can probably tell
where this is going by now.

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:33.670
- The stool samples were
negative for parasites.

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:35.410
- Raccoon roundworms are not excreted

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:36.610
by their human host.

00:09:36.610 --> 00:09:37.490
- Cameron tested.

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:40.040
- Bro, stop acting like you knew

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:43.480
about raccoon poop without
looking it up, I swear!

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:44.620
- Worms spread from his gut

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:46.930
to the rest of his body,
attacked his lungs,

00:09:46.930 --> 00:09:47.930
that's what made him scream-

00:09:47.930 --> 00:09:49.990
- I don't even care that he
knew it was raccoon poop.

00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:52.780
It's the fact that he knew
humans don't release it

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:54.000
in their own fecal matter.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:56.240
